Right.  Various colors have various uses and yellow may be the least
usefull because it grants resistance against acid and acid is a trivial
weapon compared to other attacks that happen in the dungeon.  I haven't
even looked up if YDSM grants acidity and thus immunity to stoning
because carrying a lizard happens so regularly.  Traits like reflection
of magic resistance are worth having redundantly if you can, while
traits like acidity or acid resistance are so rarely usefull and so
easily acquired it isn't worth pursuing them.

Given the choice between a mithril coat and YDSM as the only dragon
mail so far in the game, I might not even go for the extra AC if I've
have the chance to enchant the mithril enough.  Given the choice between
YDSM and almost any other color, I'd be likely to go with the other.
But there's the NetHack-standard tradeoff that YDSM grants something
that can't be gotten from eating the dragon's corpse while with
several other colors once you've eaten the corpse you've probably gotten
that intrinsic and that mail is reduced to AC-only for your purposes.

